          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %strong recollement
            situation is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            of six
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+functors"} additive functors
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo ′
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi i
                            %mo !
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi i
                          %mo *
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi j
                            %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi j
                            %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi j
                          %mo !
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo ″
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{A}'
                  \\stackrel{\overset{i^*}{\longleftarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{i_*}{\longrightarrow}}{\underset{i^!}{\longleftarrow}}}
                  \\mathcal{A}\stackrel{\overset{j_!}{\longleftarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{j^*}{\longrightarrow}}{\underset{j_*}{\longleftarrow}}}\mathcal{A}''
          %p
            among three
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+categories"} triangulated categories
            satisfying a strong list of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} exactness
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjointness
            axioms.
          %p
            The paradigmatic situation is about the categories of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaves"} abelian sheaves
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo ′
                    %mo =
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}' = Sh(C)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
